      "text": "Package construction proposal: deterministic unique safe stems (e.g. image-0001.png and image-0001.txt) in a flat archive; crop/normalize prepared static PNG/JPEG images explicitly; UTF-8 captions, one for every included image; retain originals, edited captions, crop transforms, prepared files and manifest/hash in owned storage. Local manifest contains full provenance; do not assume provider accepts arbitrary manifest members—upload archive includes only validated image/caption pairs initially, with manifest retained separately. No paths, symlinks, executable files or uncontrolled archive extraction needed because builder creates the package. Default-caption and naming decisions remain visible. Custom repositioning is applied to prepared image bytes; provider centered crop of those already-sized images is still a provider behavior to verify. Auto is computed/previewed as an app preparation policy using documented intent; if exact provider auto algorithm remains unknown, label expected crop and require explicit concrete resolution for a predictable prepared dataset. Never label an app crop as observed provider output."
    },
